{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בבגדו", :translit "b'bagdo", :gloss "in his betraying her"} {:he "כ' במסורה דין", :translit "k' b'masorah din", :gloss "twenty in the Masorah, this one"} {:he "ותתפשהו בכגדו", :translit "v'titp'seihu b'chagdo", :gloss "and she shall seize him by his cloak"} {:he "כיון שפירש טליתו עליה שוב אינו רשאי למכרה", :translit "kiyun she'pirash talito aleha shuv eino rashai l'mokrah", :gloss "once he spread his cloak over her he is no longer permitted to sell her"} {:he "דילפינן לה מבגדו דהתם שהוא בגד ממש", :translit "dilfinan lah m'bagdo d'sham she'hu bagad mamash", :gloss "we learn it from בגדו there which is an actual garment"} {:he "כיון שבגד בה שוב אינו רשאי למכרה", :translit "kiyun she'bagad bah shuv eino rashai l'mokrah", :gloss "once he betrayed her he is no longer permitted to sell her"} {:he "ודורש בבגדו בה ל' בגידה", :translit "v'doreish b'bagdo bah l'shon bagidah", :gloss "and expounds בבגדו as the language of betrayal"} {:he "יליף בגד דהתם מהכא", :translit "yaleif bagad d'sham m'ika", :gloss "he learns בגד there from here"} {:he "שגם לשם היתה בגידה", :translit "she'gam l'sham haytah bagidah", :gloss "for there too was betrayal"} {:he "לעשות צרכיו נכנס", :translit "l'asot tzerachav nichnas", :gloss "he entered to attend to his needs"} {:he "אלא שנראית לו דמות אביו", :translit "elah shenir'ot lo d'mut aviv", :gloss "but the likeness of his father appeared to him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 20, :occurrences ["בבגדו"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah linking בבגדו (betrayal) with בכגדו (cloak, Deut 25:11) and בגדו (Joseph's garment, Gen 39:12)"} {:kind :other, :note "R. Akiva reads בבגדו as cognate with בגידה (betrayal) rather than garment"}], :frame {:text "The phrase בבגדו in Exodus 21:8, concerning a master who designated a maidservant as a wife for himself or his son but then 'deals deceitfully' with her, is expounded by tannaitic authorities in the Mishnah at Kiddushin 18a. R. Elazar derives from the gezeirah shavah with בכגדו in Deuteronomy 25:11 — where the word refers to an actual garment (cloak) — that once the master spread his garment over her (an act of betrothal) he may no longer sell her. R. Akiva, who reads בבגדו as betrayal, holds the same conclusion: once he betrayed her he may not sell her. The gezeirah shavah also connects to בגדו at Genesis 39:12, the garment Joseph fled from; per Shabbat 56a, one opinion holds Judah entered to attend to his needs but the likeness of his father appeared to him — which the Ba'al HaTurim frames as betrayal on Joseph's part as well.", :sources ["Mishnah Kiddushin 18a" "Deuteronomy 25:11" "Genesis 39:12" "Shabbat 56a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 20, :occurrences ["בבגדו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "בבגדו", :refs ["Genesis 39:12" "Exodus 21:8" "2 Samuel 1:11"], :n 3, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah linking בבגדו (betrayal) with בכגדו (cloak, Deut 25:11) and בגדו (Joseph's garment, Gen 39:12)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "R. Akiva reads בבגדו as cognate with בגידה (betrayal) rather than garment", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:18:02.774672165Z", :model "glm-5.2"}